+## 📊 Comprehensive Issue Assessment
+**Issues from QA Still Present**:
+- `api-specialist-review.md` (`APPROVED`) and `message-to-reality-checker.md` overlooked the `GateWorkerRunner` zero-UUID RLS failure that `live-fullstack-proof.txt` lines 20-22 explicitly documented, because `agent/tests/gates/test_gate_runner.py` only tests against `MockSessionFactory`/`AsyncMock`.
+
+**New Issues Discovered**:
+1. **Critical - `GateWorkerRunner` fails under PostgreSQL `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` (`agent/gates/runner.py`, `p5_17a_workflow_hooks.up.sql`)**:
+   - In [runner.py](file:///home/adamoutler/kanban/agent/gates/runner.py#L71-L76,L91-L96,L134-L139,L199-L204), `poll_once`, `_load_entities`, `record_decision`, and `record_failure` all bind `RLSContext(principal_id=uuid.UUID(int=0), workspace_id=uuid.UUID(int=0), token_scopes=("admin",), aal_level=2)`.
+   - Under `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` as `kanban_app` ([p5_17a_workflow_hooks.up.sql](file:///home/adamoutler/kanban/database/migrations/sql/p5_17a_workflow_hooks.up.sql#L115-L178)), `workflow_transition_executions` and `workflow_hook_invocations` `SELECT` policies require `workspace_id = app_current_workspace_id()` AND `app_has_object_capability(issue_id, 1)`, and `issue_comments` `INSERT` requires `author_id = app_current_principal_id()` and capability 2 on `issue_id` (as directly observed in `live-fullstack-proof.txt` lines 20-23). Consequently, `GateWorkerRunner.poll_once()` returns 0 rows on live PostgreSQL, and `record_decision` / `record_failure` raise `EXECUTION_NOT_FOUND` or `InsufficientPrivilegeError`.
+2. **Critical - `GateWorkerRunner.poll_once` holds `FOR UPDATE` row locks across nested session calls (`agent/gates/runner.py`)**:
+   - [runner.py](file:///home/adamoutler/kanban/agent/gates/runner.py#L208-L276) acquires `with_for_update(skip_locked=True)` on `WorkflowHookInvocation` in `poll_once()` and awaits `self.worker.handle_dispatch(event)` before releasing/committing that transaction. Inside `handle_dispatch()`, `record_decision()` / `record_failure()` opens a second session and executes `select(WorkflowHookInvocation)...with_for_update()` ([async_gate.py](file:///home/adamoutler/kanban/kanban/workflows/async_gate.py#L304-L312,L828-L836)), which will self-deadlock on PostgreSQL once RLS permits rows to be read.
+3. **Medium - `validate_reality_checker_report` `claims_ready` boolean logic and `runner.py` status/deadline mismatches**:
+   - In [proof.py](file:///home/adamoutler/kanban/kanban/issues/proof.py#L324-L326), `claims_ready = "READY" in combined_check or bool(re.search(r"\bA\b", cert_body) or ...)` uses `or` rather than requiring `READY` explicitly when `require_ready=True` (so a report with `Grade: A` and `Status: PENDING` without `READY` would pass).
+   - In [runner.py](file:///home/adamoutler/kanban/agent/gates/runner.py#L213), `poll_once` queries `WorkflowHookInvocation.status.in_(["running", "pending_async"])` even though `ck_workflow_hook_invocations_status` does not permit `"pending_async"`, and `AgentGateDispatcher.dispatch` writes `deadline_at` to the outbox payload rather than `WorkflowHookInvocation.output_json` (relying on the `started_at + timeout_ms` fallback).
+   - Artifact commit metadata drift across the packet (`9b163f07` in `message-to-reality-checker.md` / `live-fullstack-proof.txt` vs `99dd3531dd8557a502f75466f983289aab0c6ced` in `build-or-typecheck.txt`, and `unit-test-results.txt` executed in worktree `swarm-b-kan45-final-ea722587`).
+
+**Critical Issues**:
+- `GateWorkerRunner` (`agent/gates/runner.py`) uses `uuid.UUID(int=0)` for `workspace_id` and `principal_id`, which fails under `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` (`EXECUTION_NOT_FOUND` / `InsufficientPrivilegeError`) on real PostgreSQL as `kanban_app`.
+- `GateWorkerRunner.poll_once()` holds `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` locks on `WorkflowHookInvocation` while calling `handle_dispatch()` -> `record_decision()` / `record_failure()` in a second session (`FOR UPDATE` self-deadlock).
+
+**Medium Issues**:
